// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Wave 11 (2026-09-24) — Euro Truck Simulator 2 + American Truck Simulator
// (SCS Software's "Convoy" dedicated multiplayer).
//
// Verified live against THREE independent sources, not recalled: SCS's own
// official modding wiki (modding.scssoft.com/wiki/Documentation/Tools/
// Dedicated_Server — the canonical spec for server_config.sii's real field
// names and the export_server_packages workflow), and the LsHallo/
// ets2-dedicated-convoy-server Docker image's README + entrypoint.sh +
// Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml + GitHub Actions build matrix (fetched raw
// off raw.githubusercontent.com, not just a summarized read) for the actual
// `-e KEY=` env-var surface and the two published images
// (lshallo/ets2-convoy-server, lshallo/ats-convoy-server; 79 stars, 50k+
// Docker Hub pulls, tagged release v0.4.6 pushed ~2026-07, still being
// actively pulled — a real, maintained community image, not an abandoned
// one).
//
// THE UPLOAD QUESTION (this wave's actual blocker in the prior research
// pass — see prisma/seed-wave10-games.ts's Wave 10 header): re-investigated
// from the image's own Dockerfile, not assumed. The Dockerfile COPIES a
// baked-in `default_packages/<ets2|ats>/server_packages.{sii,dat}` pair into
// `/default_packages/` at BUILD time, and entrypoint.sh runs
// `cp -n /default_packages/server_packages.{sii,dat} "$SAVEGAME_LOCATION"`
// (`-n` = no-clobber) on every container start. Consequence: the dedicated
// server boots and hosts a fully working VANILLA base-map convoy (no DLC, no
// mods) with ZERO customer-supplied file, contradicting the Wave 10 header's
// "cannot start with real content until the customer uploads..." — that
// conclusion was reached from the SCS wiki alone ("these files are necessary
// for a dedicated server to start") without checking whether the CHOSEN
// DOCKER IMAGE ships a working default pair, which this one does. A customer
// who owns paid DLC map(s) and wants them active (or wants mods) has to
// generate their OWN server_packages.sii/.dat (Game console ->
// `export_server_packages`, mirrors their exact DLC/mod ownership — SCS's own
// wiki: "these files are NOT linked to your account in any way", i.e. there
// is no way for the platform to fabricate a valid per-customer one) and drop
// it into the server's mounted save-data directory, OVERWRITING the shipped
// default, then restart — exactly the same "full file/SFTP access, no
// one-click installer" shape every other mod-driven family in this catalog
// already uses (see MOD_INFO.ets2/.ats in lib/game-mods.ts). No new
// upload feature was built for this: `lib/sftp.ts` + `lib/actions-files.ts` +
// `components/customer/files/FileBrowser.tsx` already give every customer
// real root SFTP/file-manager access to their VM, and `GAME_CONTROL.ets2/
// .ats.dataRoots` below points it at the exact bind-mounted directory
// (`/opt/ets2` / `/opt/ats` on the host) the container reads
// server_packages.sii/.dat from — see prisma/seed-wave11-games.ts's
// setupScript for the literal `-v` mount.
//
// No envKey mismatch risk (same shape as ARMAREFORGER above, not CS16): both
// images' env vars ARE the schema key, just re-prefixed ETS_/ATS_ per image
// (the entrypoint's own `getenv()` helper — read directly off
// ets_server_entrypoint.py — transparently falls back from one prefix to the
// other, but each image's own README/docker-compose.yml consistently uses
// its own game's prefix, so envKey follows that convention rather than
// relying on the fallback). Fields are keyed on server_config.sii's OWN real
// field names (lobby_name, description, welcome_message, password,
// max_players, player_damage, traffic, force_speed_limiter, name_tags,
// server_logon_token, moderator_list — confirmed off the wiki's "Server
// config paramaters" section) with `envKey` mapping each to the Docker image's
// literal `-e` name, same discipline as Valheim's `world`/`WORLD_NAME`.
//
// connection_dedicated_port/query_dedicated_port are deliberately NOT
// customer fields — same precedent as every other family, the platform's own
// IPAM (lib/ipam.ts's allocateGameForward, driven off GAME_PORT/
// GAME_EXTRA_JOIN_PORTS in lib/games.ts) owns port assignment, not the
// customer. max_players is hard-capped at 8 — SCS's own real, officially
// unsupported-beyond ceiling (raising it requires a client-side console hack
// every single player would individually have to apply — the image's own
// README: "Due to the hacky nature of the workaround I cannot provide any
// support" — not something to sell as a paid slot upsell).
//
// RCON: this game has no RCON/admin-console protocol at all (SCS's wiki:
// "As the dedicated server does not have any form or user interface..." —
// moderator promotion is entirely via `moderator_list`'s Steam64 IDs). No
// secret-generation branch was added to worker/index.ts's buildCloudInit
// (unlike Palworld/Rust/CS2/Arma's ADMIN_PASSWORD/RCON secrets) because there
// is no admin credential this image needs minted at provision time — password
// is a plain, optional join password (blank = open, matching this game's own
// documented default, NOT a required field the way Valheim's SERVER_PASS is,
// since Valheim's dedicated server refuses to start below 5 characters and
// ETS2/ATS's does not).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

